            {
                "entry_id": "d6c08367-79ce-3fb5-be84-13081637e070",
                "word": "Li",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eda8a586-9a00-355b-bcc4-a0fb217dcda1",
                        "entry_id": "d6c08367-79ce-3fb5-be84-13081637e070",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A county of Longnan, Gansu, China."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae0c522c-ff45-4c31-b854-bc28b1cb25f1",
                                "sense_id": "eda8a586-9a00-355b-bcc4-a0fb217dcda1",
                                "text": "The West Hanshui River flows through the flatland of Qishan Township east of Lixian County, Gansu Province.[…]\nZhuge launched his first northern expedition. He arrived at Qishan Mountain in Lixian County, where he set up his headquarters on the shore of the West Hanshui River."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "689c7ad2-e82f-3c11-967f-2d3088f30415",
                "word": "Li",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "59964a2c-2b5b-34d7-ab7d-1fe6500e96c4",
                        "entry_id": "689c7ad2-e82f-3c11-967f-2d3088f30415",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A river in Guangxi, China."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "894c6b60-57a8-472d-80d9-ca0027834d36",
                                "sense_id": "59964a2c-2b5b-34d7-ab7d-1fe6500e96c4",
                                "text": "After breakfast the next day, Ho Li-chih came to invite Yang Shu-tien and me to the Li River for a boat trip to another county, Yang-shuo."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9cb07dae-3a17-4faf-8c8d-ee93d7026ae9",
                                "sense_id": "59964a2c-2b5b-34d7-ab7d-1fe6500e96c4",
                                "text": "Cormorant fishing on the Li River near Kweilin. With increasingly serious water pollution, fishing with cormorants is becoming a rare sight in China."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04fa71a4-aca4-4bfb-9d44-530abcbf9480",
                                "sense_id": "59964a2c-2b5b-34d7-ab7d-1fe6500e96c4",
                                "text": "Before going home, we flew to Guilin for a meeting with environmentalists concerned about the destruction of forests and the loss of unique wildlife, and a leisurely boat trip down the Li River, which flows through a stunning landscape marked by large limestone formations that looked as if they had burst up through the landscape of the gentle countryside."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1dd4cba2-0d71-4821-9052-7c9a751ec723",
                                "sense_id": "59964a2c-2b5b-34d7-ab7d-1fe6500e96c4",
                                "text": "Days 3-5: Guilin and Yangshuo.\nMarvel at the extraordinary scenery lining the banks of the serene Li River."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9db54c99-bdcd-48d4-a992-38763a562e6e",
                                "sense_id": "59964a2c-2b5b-34d7-ab7d-1fe6500e96c4",
                                "text": "In Guilin, the second-largest city in Guangxi, Xi took a boat to inspect the ecological condition of the Li River, a popular tourist destination. The river stretches more than 400km (250 miles) through karst hills and attracts hundreds of thousands of visitors each year."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "880f3e85-094e-3451-a177-bdd148524e0c",
                "word": "li",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "9b058731-4916-4b22-b69b-fe54408b3716",
                        "entry_id": "880f3e85-094e-3451-a177-bdd148524e0c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "lis"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e62d1dee-fa4c-4449-bba3-00fbdebff629",
                        "entry_id": "880f3e85-094e-3451-a177-bdd148524e0c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "li"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78da8ac9-c172-39d7-91a9-f07acef939fb",
                        "entry_id": "880f3e85-094e-3451-a177-bdd148524e0c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The Chinese mile, a traditional unit of distance equal to 1500 chis or 150 zhangs, now standardized as a half-kilometer (500 meters)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7af13d62-4bd3-4887-8236-4b2e44d6f7e3",
                                "sense_id": "78da8ac9-c172-39d7-91a9-f07acef939fb",
                                "text": "It was a whole day's journey from I-ch'eng to Chü-wo which, in turn, is about 60 li east of Chiang Chou — one of the most important cities in southern Shansi and a center for curio-dealers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ee5009c-ce50-4636-b79a-fb82df8ea8fb",
                                "sense_id": "78da8ac9-c172-39d7-91a9-f07acef939fb",
                                "text": "In 1979, while we were conducting our archaeological work in Yucheng and Quwo, Shanxi province, I noticed another historical record in the Kuodizhi (a comprehensive account of geography written in 641), which stated that \"the ancient city of Tang was 20 li west of Yuchengxian in Jiangzhou.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c670df99-4184-4da0-a766-d60e424deacd",
                                "sense_id": "78da8ac9-c172-39d7-91a9-f07acef939fb",
                                "text": "The two gods who accompany Matsu, one with eyes that can see 1000 li⁶ and the other with ears that can hear far over the horizon, represent empathy, observation, and feeling. Government should be like Matsu, equipped with acute powers of observation; see clearly to the bottom of issues, and know how to respond."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9ae88799-ec8e-33f6-8855-8e370137c661",
                        "entry_id": "880f3e85-094e-3451-a177-bdd148524e0c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The Korean mile, a traditional unit of distance equivalent to about 393 m."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4292aef0-8c58-4d9c-9537-380d0bd76f25",
                                "sense_id": "9ae88799-ec8e-33f6-8855-8e370137c661",
                                "text": "While scaling the Laoyeling Mountains, the Chinese Worker-Peasant Red Army, under the command of Mao Ze-dong and Zhu De, was successfully stepping up the historic 25 000-li Long March in China proper, breaking through the surrounding rings formed by Chiang Kai-shek’s army."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "61976084-7458-4e41-b661-a7848b8b3138",
                        "source_entry_id": "880f3e85-094e-3451-a177-bdd148524e0c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Chinese unit of distance",
                        "target_lang_word": "li",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "li",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eddecc7d-e06c-30c6-acf4-fbf6c36efb9b",
                                        "entry_id": "1a32bb19-b311-360c-8df2-bdc7a2ba1431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chinese lengtemaat, nu gestandaardiseerd tot ½ km"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf012bef-5d7a-43e2-b379-a586d067c56d",
                                                "sense_id": "eddecc7d-e06c-30c6-acf4-fbf6c36efb9b",
                                                "text": "In de tijd van Wang Wei was een li (…), een Chinese mijl, ongeveer een derde kilometer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "db4eb5a1-d239-34da-8a7c-622e23051ccd",
                                        "entry_id": "1a32bb19-b311-360c-8df2-bdc7a2ba1431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chinese gewichtseenheid voor edelmetalen en andere kostbare stoffen, vroeger ongeveer 0.04 mg, één duizendste liang, nu gestandaardiseerd tot 50 mg"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ed583ad-e028-3ce4-af76-0a6f2fabb5e1",
                                        "entry_id": "1a32bb19-b311-360c-8df2-bdc7a2ba1431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chinese rekeneenheid, met de waarde van de gewichtseenheid li in zilver, of één duizendste taël"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce08fc9c-99de-3a9b-99ee-e25bebfdc214",
                                        "entry_id": "1a32bb19-b311-360c-8df2-bdc7a2ba1431",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chinese pot of ketel op drie holle poten"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06f9a64a-c0ef-4a94-ba58-45922687d2ad",
                                                "sense_id": "ce08fc9c-99de-3a9b-99ee-e25bebfdc214",
                                                "text": "Ze krabden kuilen in onze bloembedden, braken tweemaal een Li, die door Ludo zorgvuldig gelijmd werd, (…)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d1fb531-7cc4-4072-b6c6-54ac682edf80",
                        "source_entry_id": "880f3e85-094e-3451-a177-bdd148524e0c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Chinese unit of distance",
                        "target_lang_word": "li",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "li",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f79b24c6-266e-3bc0-8c8d-b7f0643689a3",
                                        "entry_id": "a2232f63-290e-3317-a05b-e5bf50c1267f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unité de mesure de distance chinoise qui a beaucoup varié selon les régions et les époques. La valeur fixée par le gouvernement nationaliste chinois en 1915 est de 1 800 pieds chinois (environ 576 mètres). Peut désigner aujourd’hui une distance de 500 mètres."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "824c72fd-b964-47a6-bcd2-a50f34078d4e",
                                                "sense_id": "f79b24c6-266e-3bc0-8c8d-b7f0643689a3",
                                                "text": "Wan-nien-sseu est un très vieux temple bouddhique, qui s'élève à quelques lis à peine des murailles de la ville, la courbe élégante de ses toits vernissés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2cbce4b-13cc-4536-a890-e85cf3815316",
                                                "sense_id": "f79b24c6-266e-3bc0-8c8d-b7f0643689a3",
                                                "text": "Nos mules ont d’inébranlables principes qui leur interdisent de faire plus de quarante lis à l’heure (quatre kilomètres en style français)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "50419711-dd0f-43b3-9f5b-f0e328ce369e",
                        "source_entry_id": "880f3e85-094e-3451-a177-bdd148524e0c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Chinese unit of distance",
                        "target_lang_word": "ли",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ли",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8431edb8-8ebc-343a-ac0f-6494f3177312",
                                        "entry_id": "554eeaa0-8c0c-3486-96a7-7a26a792a301",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ой ли, уж ли"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "частица, употребляется при усилении вопросительности, а также при выражении сомнения, удивления"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d51f5f4-55bb-49d0-befa-d34e97fc882d",
                                                "sense_id": "8431edb8-8ebc-343a-ac0f-6494f3177312",
                                                "text": "— Мы своё, видно, уж отгутарили… — Ой ли? — Да так уж, должно быть! Деревцо-то — оно один раз в году цветёт…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a881daa2-9f8e-34d3-b69a-bf2208cc361a",
                                        "entry_id": "554eeaa0-8c0c-3486-96a7-7a26a792a301",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "вряд ли, едва ли, едва ли не, чуть ли не, навряд ли, мало ли, то ли дело, шутка ли, что ли, чёрт ли, есть ли"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "частица (в некоторых выражениях, первоначально бывших вопросительными, а теперь потерявших такое значение), теперь со значением сомнения, неуверенности, нерешительности и т. п."
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fc0fbca-5edc-4ab5-b6e2-3c7def4be217",
                                                "sense_id": "a881daa2-9f8e-34d3-b69a-bf2208cc361a",
                                                "text": "— Мабудь, и встренемся когда, — сказал Пугачёв, по-простецки обнимая рыбьего человека. — Только навряд ли. Горазд далече до тебя."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fab257a2-add2-4f1a-a081-3e2c53d202ad",
                                                "sense_id": "a881daa2-9f8e-34d3-b69a-bf2208cc361a",
                                                "text": "— Так что ж, матушка, по рукам, что ли? — говорил Чичиков."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ddd7dba-858d-41e1-ba5a-be13e5759f49",
                                                "sense_id": "a881daa2-9f8e-34d3-b69a-bf2208cc361a",
                                                "text": "Вы на веку своём едва ли // Таких ночей десяток насчитали…"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ли",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
